"""Source list for the //weld:runtime py_library.

Extracted verbatim from weld/BUILD.bazel, which sat exactly at the 400-line
cap -- so every new runtime module breached it, and the enumerated source
list is the only part big enough to be worth moving. Entries and their order
are unchanged, so //weld:runtime is the same target it was. Same extraction
pattern as weld/tests/strategy_tests.bzl.

A new weld/*.py module must be added here to reach the Bazel target. Keep it
alphabetical, as the rest of the list is.

One deliberate absence: ``__init__.py``. It is declared once, by
``//weld:package_init``, which every py_ target in the package depends on --
including ``:runtime``. Two declarations would be harmless to Bazel (the same
source artifact either way) and misleading to a reader, because the rule this
package has to hold is that *no* target reaches weld/ without the real file;
a per-target srcs entry cannot say that, and a shared dep can. See the comment
on that target for what the second treatment costs (bd p07k).
"""

